Introducing "engines" in `package.json` for `msal-node` to update `Node.js` version support.

```javascript
 "engines" : {
    "node" : ">=14.0.0"
  }
```

According to Bloomreach guideline, `site-development` module contains repository data definitions pertaining to the delivery web application used only for development and testing purposes. These definitions usually don't end up on production systems

Folder hst:workspace contains data which maintained by the webmaster and different between development and production environment. We do not want push our local testing data on this folder into production environment so we ideally this should be considered as development data.

@smanivasag There is one important change to make this movement working is that we need to update file `hcm-module.yaml ` to change `site: hee-cms-platform` into `site: hee`. Because this site name must be identical to the name declared in file `hcm-site.yaml`

